 "preferred_name": "Accelerated failure time models",
 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "A class of survival-analysis regression models in which the covariates act multiplicatively on the time until an event occurs.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A parametric model in survival analysis that is an alternative to proportional hazards models. Instead of multiplying the hazard, it assumes a covariate speeds up or slows down the course of the event being studied by a constant factor.",
